WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.120
The Cathedral of Notre-Dame at Reims.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.520
French kings have been crowned 
in this location for generations.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.360
However, due to the sudden 
death of Charles VI,

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.730
no one sits upon the French throne.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.530
England saw this as an opportunity,

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:22.860
and forcibly held a crowning ceremony 
in the cathedral for their king, Henry VI,

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:27.210
{meijitsu}in an attempt to legitimize 
their rule of France.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.960
The crowning ceremony must be held for 
Princess Charlotte as soon as possible.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.280
For hear to reach the cathedral,

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:40.080
they must first liberate Orléans 
to secure a safe path to Reims.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.940
The clash in Orléans intensified,

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.150
as the tide of battle 
shifted in England's favor.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.080
Alençon!

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.020
Where's the cavalry?!

00:00:50.020 --> 00:01:00.330
<b>#05 Proof of Purity</b>

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.570
Jeanne d'Arc and the Alchemist Knight

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.410
Not enough troops.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.990
It's not my fault.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:26.300
I knew there wouldn't, but...

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.880
It's not my fault.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:28.890
How's it going?

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.250
All right, I guess.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.210
I didn't know you were so short on troops!

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.880
Let's go!

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.810
We can liberate Orléans on our own!

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.600
You're really strong.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:55.600
But you can only remain 
Ulysses for three minutes.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.600
And it takes half a day to recover.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:58.810
It's impossible.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.950
Our only hope is...

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.520
Please wait, Lady Richemont!

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.380
Brother!

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.010
Hi, Richemont.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.520
Will you call us again?

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:26.810
Of course.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.270
I hope it's just the two of us next time.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.390
Oh, you're so cute.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:34.080
Please don't make it hard for me.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.670
My love belongs to all ladies out there.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.360
Welcome back, Richemont.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.140
I want to borrow 2,000 soldiers.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.370
You've been gone for so long.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.290
Why don't you enjoy some of our great wines?

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.920
I sent the request many times, 
but haven't received any reply,

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.770
so I came here in person.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:03.620
My dear little sister, 
being a ruler makes you very busy.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.280
I'm sorry. I forgot something.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.950
Oh!

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.950
Here, here, here!

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.920
Bless you.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.130
I hate wars.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:50.470
It creates neither love nor art.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.160
Nothing comes of it.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.230
It will create stories of heroes.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.480
I hate those, too.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.850
The French royal family allowed the Bretons 
to move to this land centuries ago.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:06.200
Have you forgotten our beautiful 
history of loyalty and knighthood

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.490
that has ensued since the 6th century?

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:11.400
You promised to send 
soldiers for the royal family,

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.250
yet all you've done is postpone that promise!

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.070
If England wins the war,

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:20.000
all the factions that assisted the French 
royal family would be severely punished.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.830
We're asking for the soldiers 
to prevent that from happening.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.060
How about a glass of wine?

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:30.650
<i>He's hopeless.</i>

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.850
Brittany is an independent kingdom.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:52.120
It does not belong to France.

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:56.310
You are trying to lead 
this nation to its doom.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.420
We cannot allow that.

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:03.590
Such a sinful body.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.790
I'll go, too!

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.200
You have my thanks.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:34.970
We have to help our best client's family.

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:37.770
I didn't think Brittany 
had already fallen this low.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:42.080
When the nation is in disarray, 
so too are hearts of the people.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.830
I guess it's to be expected, 
with a ruler like that.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:47.210
He's waiting to ally with 
the side that comes out on top.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:50.940
No, he's just afraid of making a decision.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:54.600
He lacks courage of siding 
with France or England.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:57.480
Just procrastinating on 
a decision that must be made.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:01.260
May I tell you a story about your brother?

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:06.480
Lord Bedford made a demand to us again.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.610
"Hand over Richemont."

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.760
He's obsessed with her.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:11.710
It's a pain.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:15.870
If you hand her over, it would 
mean we have allied with England.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:16.760
Huh?

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:19.980
She's my sister!

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:22.320
How can I hand her over to that man?

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:25.250
Someone who's gentle 
is more suitable for her.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:30.220
I'll use every scheme, tactic, 
and trickery at my disposal

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.760
to protect Richemont, 
no matter what it takes!

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:37.400
He's an indecisive person as you said.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.640
I guess you can't call him a good ruler.

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:45.010
But still, he can be brave, for you.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:49.880
{sonna}I hope you can understand that part of him.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.290
Pull harder!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.470
We did it!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.220
Mythological sword Joyeuse, huh?

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:12.040
It's just a worn-out sword.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.560
How rude!

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:17.680
It's the sword with a distinguished history 
that symbolizes French royal authority!

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.470
When Jeanne brandishes the sword,

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:22.810
it might draw out loyal knights 
from all over France!

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:25.160
Do you really think it'll work out that well?

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:27.480
I don't think you can even 
slice a raddish with this.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:28.730
You're such a fool.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:32.280
That's a Philosopher's Stone which 
has been forged in the shape of a sword.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.110
What?

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:35.450
We're in middle of something!

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:37.360
M-My apologies.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.500
Count La Tremoille is requesting a meeting.

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:46.350
I made a wrong assumption that 
there was an uprising in the castle.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:49.320
I cannot even begin to express how 
regretful I am for fleeing the castle,

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:51.660
leaving Your Majesty behind.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:54.590
Yeah, right. Didn't you hire an assassin?

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:55.970
An assassin?

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.840
I heard the man named 
Maugris bit off his tongue

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:00.970
and died after he was captured.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:04.150
Where's your proof that I hired him?

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.360
So what do you want?

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:10.440
To be clear, I will not restore 
your title of Grand Chamberlain.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.820
Please take a look at this.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:19.270
This is...

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:32.630
Virginity test?!

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.260
That bastard La Tremoille!

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:41.020
He imbued the Church with the idea 
that Jeanne slept with the devil

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:42.840
to obtain her superhuman powers.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:48.020
Don't tell me you agreed to the test.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.900
Of course not!

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:53.520
If La Tremoille is involved,

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.030
he would turn white into black.

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:57.930
They may even rape her.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:14.750
If only I were able to bring 
the troops back with me,

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:17.420
our situation may have been different.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.550
I'm sorry.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.850
You've always been too 
serious for your own good.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.560
But I'm glad...

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:27.680
that you're still the same 
Richemont that I know.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:29.750
Montmorency...

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.650
Don't burden yourself with everything.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.840
Let me take off some of your burden.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:34.620
All right?

00:10:55.960 --> 00:11:00.430
Why is the Domremy girl 
running from the virginity test?

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.840
Isn't it because she has something to hide?

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:07.470
Her Majesty shouldn't be covering it up!

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.530
General Richemont, who we counted on,

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:13.860
also failed to bring soldiers back with her!

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:19.630
Furthermore, the man named 
Montmorency who entered the palace

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:23.600
was a black magician who was considered 
to be a heretic by the Church!

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:26.960
The French royal family has become corrupt!

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:30.250
From the moment Count La Tremoille left!

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:34.120
I must regain my title of 
Grand Chamberlain soon.

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:36.970
The royal family will 
be overthrown without me.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:39.840
When I return to the castle,

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:43.860
I'll have to add that winged fairy 
to my stuffed fairy collection!

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:48.730
No.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:49.400
But...

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:50.520
Absolutely not!

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.490
Jeanne blames herself for not 
being able to assemble soldiers,

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.320
and depart for Orléans.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:07.910
So she wants to take the virginity test.

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:12.970
We can't get out of our current crisis 
by using Joyeuse to boost morale.

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:15.940
Not until this situation is settled.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.910
I absolutely won't allow it!

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.540
Please, Richemont!

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:26.090
Ask the Duke of Brittany
 again to send us troops!

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:31.610
Jeanne.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:36.380
I have led you to a thorny path.

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:37.380
I'm sorry.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:41.260
No, you saved me.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:44.950
My fate was to die, 
but you gave me a new life.

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:46.950
Don't apologize.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.810
The Duke of Brittany is a coward!

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:54.270
Just waiting to see if France 
or England comes out on top...

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:56.140
He's practically a parasite!

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:59.530
If Brittany hadn't refused to be annexed,

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:01.660
this war would've been over long ago.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:05.340
Brittany is a nation of Bretons.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:08.600
We do not need the French royal family 
telling us what to do about annexation.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:11.070
Is that your personal opinion?

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:13.210
E-Everyone is saying it!

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:16.480
I don't call all the shots 
at the royal family.

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:20.090
Your mother was also behaving like a parasite

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:22.360
when she married the English king 
after the French king passed away.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.070
I understand.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.100
There's nothing left for me to say.

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.200
Suit yourself!

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:41.300
I promise...

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.210
I'll keep protecting you.

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:46.540
I'll never get married.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:50.330
Just as legendary knights swore 
their allegiance to noblewomen,

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:53.470
let's live a life where we 
can maintain our inner purity.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.600
Montmorency...

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:56.650
Yeah.

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.690
I'm so happy!

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:16.500
Is it true that Richemont resigned?

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:18.330
Yes.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:27.760
That little girl in the 
battlefield sure has grown.

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:38.020
<i>I didn't run away because 
I was afraid of losing my purity.</i>

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:42.390
<i>I was afraid that I couldn't 
offer my purity to you.</i>

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:46.030
<i>But you're no longer...</i>

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:56.350
I will assign someone else 
appropriate for the general's post.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:59.180
Tell Xaintrailles and others not to worry.

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:01.340
I'll do something about 
the additional soldiers...

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:02.730
I'm out.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:03.540
What?

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:06.050
I can't lead my men to their deaths.

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:07.670
Sorry.

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:19.880
It was only for a short while, 
but thank you for protecting me.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.470
You can have this.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.420
I'm counting on you, archangel!

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.630
Okay.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:58.330
The archangel will now deliver God's message 
regarding the maiden of Domremy!

00:15:58.330 --> 00:15:59.370
I object!

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:02.100
That's not an angel.

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:06.110
It's merely a rare fairy, 
recorded in ancient documents!

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:09.070
God's messenger, or molded documents...

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.860
Which one would you believe?

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:18.390
We'll have the answer 
once she takes the virginity test!

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:24.780
Jeanne is risking her life 
trying to end the war!

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:27.380
Don't be fooled by the 
black magician's words!

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:33.880
Damn it...

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:39.190
Wait! If you attack now, 
it'll turn into a real uprising.

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:53.880
Emergency!

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:54.730
It's an emergency!

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:55.830
Montmorency is...

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:07.420
Jeanne?

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:20.990
Heretics can't go to Heaven.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:23.720
Montmorency, the flames of Hell
are waiting for you.

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:25.830
You're the ones who will burn there.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:36.200
We have him as insurance.

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:38.020
You trash.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:56.000
This is hardly a surprise.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:58.970
It's what happens when you 
try to act cool when you're weak.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.490
Reflect on your mistake.

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:06.980
If you'd only take the virginity test...

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.850
Shut your dirty mouth!

00:18:09.510 --> 00:18:13.660
It won't take ten seconds 
to cut off all your heads.

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:16.860
But I won't.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:20.240
Tomorrow... no, it can be right after this.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.730
I'll take the virginity test!

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.520
Jeanne won't kill people.

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:35.300
Jeanne lost her little sister to war.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:40.180
She knows that life lost 
would be gone forever.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:44.280
That's why she decided 
to use her power... her life,

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:47.140
only to protect.

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:49.750
Tell me...

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:52.150
Does she look like a demon to you?

00:18:58.600 --> 00:18:59.720
Montmorency!

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:00.870
Jeanne?

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:07.910
Can we really take the Joyeuse with us?

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:12.660
I should become Ulysses 
myself and head to Orléans...

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:15.580
But my role as princess 
makes that impossible.

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:24.760
New knights have assembled 
thanks to the Joyeuse,

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:26.760
so Jeanne has to hold on to it.

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:27.700
Right.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.290
Knights sure are impressive.

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:33.230
Will we really be useful?

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:37.150
You fools! Even kids like Jeanne are fighting!

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:38.400
You're right.

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:40.280
We're the Maiden Volunteer Corps!

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:43.230
We'll devote our lives to 
Jeanne and fight England!

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:45.160
It'll be the most powerful force!

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:49.500
One person can only be equipped with
one Philosopher's Stone at a time.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:50.350
Okay!

00:19:50.350 --> 00:19:51.450
That's the rule.

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:52.170
Okay!

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:56.300
Because you only possess 
half of a Philosopher's Stone,

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:59.040
you were only able to absorb the
Joyeuse's power for a brief moment.

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:01.440
But you can only do that once.

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:03.430
You can't depend on the Joyeuse again.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.520
That's enough.

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:10.150
Sheesh! You both treat 
Philosopher's Stones too lightly.

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:23.000
Montmorency!

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:35.120
Let's keep our focus.

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:37.520
Ending the war against England...

00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:40.480
That is the first step 
towards ending all wars

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:43.840
and turning the world into 
a utopia, Montmorency.

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:45.200
Actually,

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:48.350
maybe I should call you by your 
full name for occasions like this.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.390
Gilles de Montmorency-Laval.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:54.380
Or would you prefer a shorter version?

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:56.100
Gilles de Rais?

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.600
You can call me whatever you want.

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:00.990
Let's get going!

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:01.770
Yeah!

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:05.000
Onward to Orléans!

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:34.930
<b>#06 Ashes to Ashes</b>

00:23:20.980 --> 00:23:23.480
As Jeanne rushes toward Orléans,

00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:24.960
an incredible foe stands before her.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.380
Its name is Ulysses Noire,

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:27.710
the black Ulysses!

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:29.870
Episode 6: "Ashes to Ashes."

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:34.970
Jeanne! Show them that the size of 
breast doesn't equal fighting power!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Surprisingly useful French lesson</b>

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>"Shut your dirty mouth!"</b>

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Use it when someone says something horrible 
to make them stand down using words!</b>
